invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser_ext.c
catches: srv_test
reason: read_psk_binders admits a binders list under 33 bytes, which RFC 9846
  §4.2.11 bounds at <33..2^16-1> because one entry costs its length byte
  plus 32. An empty list runs no walk, so the per-entry floor never reads
  it, and a pre_shared_key offering identities and no binder at all parses.
  test/srv_parser_tests.h sends that empty list.

--- old
    if (e->err || binders_len < PSK_BINDERS_MIN || binders_len > rb_left(e)) {
--- new
    if (e->err || binders_len > rb_left(e)) {
